#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:5
#: 7b45d628141a4ba69a498d4bd8ce1884
msgid "Branching and Committing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:7
#: e7ce422a117144d694d7b5d3f2ec47c5
msgid "**Branches** are a way to isolate different paths of development, which can then be combined (aka \"merged\") into a single branch (often named \"master\"). Refer to `this short guide <http://gitready.com/beginner/2009/01/25/branching-and-merging.html>`__ or the resources in the :ref:`Learning Git <where-to-get-the-code_learning_git>` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:11
#: 2896f941c7384410b7c6bfbf64a3abdf
msgid "**Commits** record changes to the code along with a description and the author's name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:13
#: 83fc57ffaf084b14a0a21702c64469fd
msgid "This page describes how to create a branch and add some commits. The instructions show the command line interface but all of the :ref:`recommended GUI tools <git-install>` can also perform these functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:17
#: 1249dbee043a4862aa5e8934baf4a8d4
msgid "Creating a Branch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:19
#: 262ea659750b4ae2b6820ee08597a48f
msgid "open a terminal window and cd to the ardupilot directory of your :ref:`clone <git-clone>` and checkout the master branch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:25
#: 5a0e0bf9286c479abe4ff8b62f10c55a
msgid "the new branch will be a copy of the current branch so ensure your :ref:`clone's <git-clone>` master branch is up-to-date with (aka :ref:`rebased on <git-rebase>`) `ArduPilot/master <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__. If you have just :ref:`forked <git-fork>` and :ref:`cloned <git-clone>` your repo then it should already be up-to-date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:28
#: 8ca301b6832e43a5ab7149c89f749dcb
msgid "decide on a branch name and create the new branch.  The name is up to you but it can be helpful to choose a short descriptive name. The branch name used for this tutorial is \"ardupilot_git_tutorial\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:34
#: b4de00f90b83436c8a9ef828bd0df2e7
msgid "Change some code. For this tutorial, open the **Tools/GIT_Test/GIT_Success.txt** in your preferred text editor, and put your name at the end of the file then save the file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:38
#: e92ceda7e20b4621a0a6d733dda0da37
msgid "See that you have changed the files by checking the status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:44
#: bd5ab36c5b86407a8f5ac354ab724550
msgid "**Stage** and **Commit** your work to the branch to record your changes to your :ref:`clone <git-clone>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:51
#: cca4679015d14ed9bcbaa6cd7c515477
msgid "In this case, the subject line of the commit is simply \"Tools: added name to GIT_Success.txt\" but see :ref:`here <submitting-patches-back-to-master>` for more detailed information on conventions for commits that you expect to be integrated into `ArduPilot/master <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:55
#: 7d42c6eb142741ef94c018f3a710044c
msgid "**Push** the new branch from your local :ref:`clone <git-clone>` to your :ref:`fork <git-fork>` on GitHub. This will copy your work on your local branch to a new branch on GitHub. Pushing branches is a precondition for collaborating with others on GitHub or for submitting patches back to the official releases.  It is assumed \"origin\" is the remote name of your :ref:`fork <git-fork>` on GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/git-branch.rst:64
#: c331a17aaf3945c19f1a31192b1d338b
msgid "Congratulations! This is bulk of the normal process you'd follow when working on code to submit back to the official project. The next step is to :ref:`submit a pull request <submitting-patches-back-to-master>` so your changes can be considered for addition to the main project."
msgstr ""

